Found it, and it isn't the start chain — it's a latent bug the fix exposed. Before this change the entry path never ran past `ALREADY_LIVE`, so it had never reached the roster wiring.

## What the log is telling you

The sequence is: `Joined the room` (LiveKit connected, mic published — the image confirms that too), then the assertion, then `Could not get into the live room`, then `Closing the room`.

That assertion comes from `Future<void> attach() => _participants.initialize.runAsync();`. `ParticipantsManager.initialize` is built with `Command.createSyncNoParamNoResult` — a **synchronous** command — and command_it asserts when `runAsync` is used on one. `attach()` is awaited inside `ActiveBroadcastSession.start()`, so the assertion propagated out of `start()`, the manager treated the entry as failed, closed the freshly joined room, and the editor correctly stayed put because `session.value` was never set. Your "Finalize Broadcast" label is simply `step == started` with no entry yet.

## The fix

[active_broadcast_session.dart](apps/mobile/lib/features/broadcast/session/active_broadcast_session.dart) now runs the sync command the way a sync command is run:

```dart
Future<void> attach() async => _participants.initialize.run();
```

`initialize` only wires the socket subscriptions and pipes them into `_fetchParticipants` (the async command that does the actual roster pull), so nothing is lost by not awaiting it — that fetch reports its own failures through its own error filter, and `attach()` still returns a `Future<void>` so the `LiveRoster` contract and the session's ordering (connect, then attach) are unchanged.

I checked the other `runAsync` call sites in the live path (`leaveOrEnd`, profile/feed `fetch`, permission prompts, `_fetchParticipants`): all target async commands, so this was the only mismatch. `deleteDraft.runAsync(...)` in the editor is also an async command.

## Verification

`flutter analyze` → No issues found. `flutter test test/features/broadcast` → 97 passed, 1 skipped (the ObjectBox-dependent editor page test). No API change was needed.

Hot restart the app and press **Finalize Broadcast** on the draft that is already committed: it should skip the go-live (step is `started`), resume a token, join, attach the roster, then route through [live_session_init_page.dart](apps/mobile/lib/features/broadcast/pages/live_session_init_page.dart) into [live_session_shell.dart](apps/mobile/lib/features/broadcast/layouts/live_session_shell.dart). If a room is still open from the failed attempt, the same press resumes it rather than creating another. Worth knowing: this now takes the path the earlier failure masked, so the live screens are getting their first real run — the roster and the ended flow are the two spots to watch.
